{"id":"u-7abe810f-646b-47fe-bb21-9295bd41e423","src":"community","title":"Strength & Power for the Ring","author":"Kamil","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/UPztRg-boxing-3-timeweek-stregth-traning","desc":"MAIN LIFTS — 3-WEEK WAVE PERIODIZATION + DELOAD\nMain lifts (Front Squat, Bench Press and Trap Bar Deadlift) follow a 3-week wave. Increase intensity while reducing the number of sets: Week 1 at approximately 75%, Week 2 at 80%, and Week 3 at 85% of 1RM. Keep 2–3 reps in reserve (RIR 2–3, RPE ≤8). Week 4 is a deload: use approximately 60% of the working weight and half the usual sets. Increase weights in the next cycle only if Week 3 was completed with good technique and no excessive fatigue.\n\nACCESSORIES — DOUBLE PROGRESSION + DELOAD\nStart at the lower end of the prescribed rep range. Keep the same weight and add one rep per set each week. Once all sets reach the upper rep limit with clean technique and RIR 2–3, increase the load by the prescribed increment and restart at the lower rep limit. If you miss the target, repeat the same load and progression step. Week 4: reduce the load to approximately 60% and perform half the usual sets.\n \nWEEK 5 — NEW TRAINING CYCLE\nAfter the deload, review your performance and recovery from the previous 4-week block. Do not perform a mandatory 1RM test. Estimate your current 1RM from recent working sets if needed, or keep your existing training max if progress is unclear.\n\nIf Week 3 was completed with good technique and RPE ≤8, increase the working weights for the next cycle: Bench Press +2.5 kg, Front Squat +5 kg, and Trap Bar Deadlift +5 kg. Start the new 3-week wave at the prescribed Week 1 intensity.\n\nFor accessories, increase the load by the prescribed increment only if all sets reached the upper rep limit with clean technique. Otherwise, keep the same weight and continue progressing.\n\nPrioritize boxing performance, recovery, and bar speed. If fatigue or performance issues persist after the deload, repeat the previous training weights or reduce training volume instead of forcing progression.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Strength","Athletics"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":80,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-11-01T20:00:12.265Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Strength & Power A 75%","Speed","Strength & Power B 75%"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Hang Clean","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Box Jump","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":75,"x":8}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":75,"x":8}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Rotational Landmine Push Press","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"External Rotations","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pallof Press","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pogo Jump","sets":[{"r":20,"x":3}]},{"n":"Vertical Jump","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Medball Chest Throw","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Medball Rotational Throw","sets":[{"r":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Medball Slam","sets":[{"r":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Clap Push Up","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Inverted Row","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Nordic Curl","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Trap Bar Deadlift","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":75,"x":6}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Push Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pendlay Row","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Hang Clean","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Box Jump","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":80,"x":6}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":80,"x":6}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Rotational Landmine Push Press","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"External Rotations","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pallof Press"